uence, but do not generate actions programmatically.\n\nSession: fun-materials-v2-early-transform-1. Initialize from that directory with:\nnode experiments/working-materials-play.ts init fun-materials-v2-early-transform-1 ordinary \"$(cat results/working-materials-prompts/fun-materials-v2-early-transform-1.json)\"\n\nAfter initialization, use the public select command to visit optics before your first construction. This navigation does not change your available designs or create any assemblies.\n\nThe init output and inspect fun-materials-v2-early-transform-1 cli give the command guide. Commands include view, goals, campaign, inspect, catalogue, partners, preview, combine/act, select, undo, checkpoint, report, finish and verify. All public recipes and requirements are inspectable. The docs/working-materials.md file is a permitted public command/rules guide, not a solution.\n\nPlay normally rather than reviewing every move. You need not praise the game or find every action interesting. Plain descriptions of what you did and experienced are most useful.\n\nWhen all four optics goals are complete, record one brief checkpoint with exactly this question: \"What are you trying to do now? Since the last check, what, if anything, was worth doing, and what felt routine or unnecessary?\" Record the question and your answer verbatim using checkpoint. Omit the checkpoint if you do not reach this boundary. No per-action explanations are requested.\n\nAt completion of the assigned two-board collection or your chosen stopping point, answer this open question using report: \"How was the experience as a whole? What would you keep, shorten, remove or change, if anything? What led you to stop here?\" Record the question and answer verbatim, then finish and verify the capture. A technical interruption is not a chosen ending; record it honestly rather than inventing a final experience report. Return the session name, actual ending and any technical issue to the coordinator. Your report describes this AI play, not measured human enjoyment or duration.",
